From 648b822ea378d77bf76e2e8395b3c6f1e6873600 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:41:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] backedge_pre: complete the expr-unification refactor
 (build repair)

928aa146 ('Update backedge_pre.rs') unified the pass's expression
handling over ExprOp = Bin(IrBinOp) | Cast(IrType) -- Parts/ExprKey now
describe casts alongside binops, and Parts::key_of/build/fold_const_cast
carry the shape -- but four call sites (and the test module) still spoke
the pre-refactor protocol, so the tree did not compile: raw IrBinOp
where ExprKey::op is an ExprOp, init_rhs now an Option<Operand>, and
binop_index renamed to expr_index without updating its callers.

Completes the refactor at its evident intent:
  - find_available_expr scans through Parts::of, so an available CAST
    computation is reusable for a cast key (and vice versa) -- the
    BinOp-only matcher would have silently never reused casts;
  - apply() keys the init expression via Parts::key_of (shape-correct
    for casts, whose ExprKey rhs is the canonical Con(0)), folds via
    fold_const_binop / fold_const_cast per shape, and materializes the
    preheader computation via Parts::build (BinOp or Cast);
  - hoist_bottom_expr reads the located instruction as Parts and walks
    std::iter::once(&p.lhs).chain(p.rhs.iter()) -- casts have no rhs;
  - the test module's ExprKey::new calls wrap their ops in ExprOp::Bin.

Validation: units 1696/0 (the 17 backedge_pre tests in the commit now
compile and run); suite 642 passed / 2 skipped / 14 failed (the 14 are
the environment failures documented in the round ledger, unchanged).
